# What `docker build` sends to the daemon when the context is the repository root, which is how
# packaging/docker/Dockerfile expects to be built:
#
#   docker build -f packaging/docker/Dockerfile --target runner -t concentus-runner .
#
# Everything below is either build output the image rebuilds for itself, or something that has no
# business inside an image (a checkout's history, its secrets, a machine's data). Leaving
# node_modules in alone turns a ten-megabyte context into a gigabyte one, and a Windows
# node_modules copied into a Linux build breaks the install it was meant to save.
.git
.claude
.env
.env.local

node_modules
**/node_modules
**/target
**/dist
**/data
**/playwright-report
**/test-results
apps/desktop/release
apps/desktop/resources

# Not part of the jar: the site, the docs, the package-manager manifests and CI.
apps/website
docs
bucket
.github
